    "agentReply": "experiment_1.peer-b.direct\n\n`open` validates sandbox/cwd ([622\u2013631](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:622)). For a new vault, it preflights app-server startup, initialization, `account/read`, and `model/list` ([666\u2013674](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:666)), then saves `threadId:null` or a supplied existing ID without resuming it ([678\u2013703](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:678)). Reopening an unborn vault returns; an existing thread is initialized/resumed ([728\u2013752](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:728)).\n\nOn first `send`/`ask`, `_birth_or_resume` calls `thread/start` when the ID is null, assigning the returned ID **in memory** ([847\u2013857](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:847)).\n\nPersistence follows successful turn completion and reconciliation ([879\u2013885](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:879), [946\u2013952](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:946)); `save_state` writes temporary JSON and replaces the state file ([609\u2013614](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:609)).\n\nA first-turn timeout ([485\u2013491](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:485)) or reconciliation exception ([521\u2013534](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:521)) can therefore leave the saved ID null despite server-side creation or processing. Null does not establish non-execution; retrying can create another thread. `ask`\u2019s later text mismatch occurs **after saving** ([952\u2013959](/home/hruzam/ia-sync/zsh/ai/tunnel-codex.py:952)).\n\nThis is static analysis; no runtime failure was observed.",
